# Data
# Anchored to the repo root: v1 dumped scratch PDFs there. Unanchored, this pattern would
# also swallow knowledge/projects/*/papers/*.pdf — the seed corpus Phase 1 commits on
# purpose (task 1.9) — since a gitignore pattern with no leading slash matches at any depth.
/*.pdf
extracted_images/
chroma_db/

# Models
gemma-3-12b-mlx/
gemma3-12b-int4/

# Secrets
# Anchored to the repo root: this is v1's API-token directory. B18 moved v2's design
# tokens to config/tokens/ believing an unanchored `tokens/` couldn't reach them — it was
# wrong. A gitignore pattern with no leading slash matches a directory of that name at ANY
# depth, so config/tokens/ was silently excluded from every commit since Phase 0's first
# push, and every CI run since has been missing it (7 failing tests, `config/tokens/*.json
# not found`). Anchoring is what B18 should have done originally.
/tokens/
.env

# Python
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# System
.DS_Store
# Temp render files
rendered_slides/
renderer_test_output/
test_*.pptx
test_*.png

# --- v2 ---
# Per-build artifacts (IR versions, verdicts, renders) — plan §4
runs/
# Ingested documents. Derived from knowledge/projects/*/papers/, which IS tracked, so a
# clone rebuilds this with `autodeck knowledge ingest`. Committing it would put a large,
# model-version-dependent artifact in the repo and — worse — let a stale store outlive the
# PDF it was derived from, which is exactly the drift the hash check exists to catch.
corpus/
# GATE 1a spot-check renders (~5 MB of page images). Same reasoning as corpus/: derived
# from the tracked PDFs and regenerable with `autodeck knowledge spotcheck`. A committed
# sheet would also go stale silently on the next re-ingest, showing boxes that no longer
# match the citations — worse than no sheet, because it looks authoritative.
# spikes/gate0/ IS tracked: those artifacts need PowerPoint to judge and cannot be
# regenerated by anyone who does not run the code.
spikes/gate1a/
# Eval outputs; the harness and fixtures under evals/ ARE tracked
evals/out/
# Environments
.venv/
# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
# Licensed font binaries — see the Phase 0 font spike before committing any
fonts/*.ttf
fonts/*.otf
# ...and the licence text that scripts/install-dev-fonts.sh places beside them. The OFL
# asks that the licence travel with the font files; since the files themselves are not
# committed, a licence sitting here alone would imply vendored fonts this repo does not
# carry. The script writes both together into a working fonts/, which is where the
# obligation actually applies.
fonts/*-LICENSE.txt

